reliable complete\ninformation. No warranties of any kind are expressed\nor implied. Readers acknowledge that the author is\nnot engaging in the rendering of legal, financial,\nmedical or professional advice.\nBy reading this document, the reader agrees that\nunder no circumstances are we responsible for any\nlosses, direct or indirect, which are incurred as a\nresult of the use of information contained within this\ndocument, including, but not limited to, —errors,\nomissions, or inaccuracies.\n \nTABLE OF CONTENTS\nINTRODUCTION\nCHAPTER 1: WHA T IS NLP?\nCHAPTER 2: HOW PEOPLE THINK\nCHAPTER 3: ELEMENTS OF NLP\nCHAPTER 4: PREDETERMINED ELEMENTS OF NLP\nCHAPTER 5: IMPLEMENTING NLP IN YOUR LIFE\nCHAPTER 6: WHERE YOU SHOULD USE NLP\nCHAPTER 7: NLP AND HYPNOSIS\nCHAPTER 8: SOME MIND CONTROL TECHNIQUES\nCHAPTER 9: SOME MORE TECHNIQUES OF MIND CONTROL\nCHAPTER 10: TIPS T O IMPROVE COMMUNICA TION\nCHAPTER 1 1: NLP FOR CHILDREN\nCHAPTER 12: THE IMPOR TANCE OF SMALL T ALK\nCHAPTER 13: SELF-HYPNOSIS\nCHAPTER 14: MIND CONTROL WITH THE WORKPLACE\nCHAPTER 15: NLP MYTHS\nCHAPTER 16: USING MIND CONTROL IN RELA TIONSHIPS\nKEY HIGHLIGHTS\nCONCLUSION\nFREE BONUS\n \n \nINTRODUCTION\nIn this day and age of cut throat competition, it becomes all\nthe more important for people to utilize their full mental\ncapacity in order to achieve the heights of success. Not doing\nso migh t result in being left behind, while the competition\nforges ahead.\nAll human beings have the potential to multitask and can\nfinish arduous tasks within a matter of minutes. But not\neverybody is able to do so, and only those that truly\ncapitalizes on their mental abilities, by training their minds\nto delve into the depths of knowledge, will be able to attain\ndue success!\nThere will always be winners and those that will look up to\nthem in envy . If everybody were to be the former , then we\nwould end up in a world where no competition would exist.\nHowever , the main goal for most humans is to be a winner\nand leave the competition behind.\nSo what is it that helps these winners achieve the kind of\nsuccess that they experience in life and what do the others\nlack? W ell, the answer lies in three simple letters, NLP .\nNLP stands for Neuro Linguistic Programming and refers to\nconcept that allows people to control their own and other\npeople’ s minds, while influenci ng thought and behavior; to\nattain more out of life.\nIn this book, we will look at the meaning of NLP, explore its\ncore concepts and also see how you can implement it in your\nday-to-day life. There are specific chapters dedicated to\nunderstanding the concept of NLP, exploring its meaning,\nsteps to implement in your life and also a few tips on small\ntalk.\nI thank you for choosing this book and hope you have a good\ntime reading it.\nLet us begin.\n \nCHAPTER 1 \nWHAT IS NLP? \nNLP is a core concept of psychology . It stands for Neuro\nLinguistic Programming.\nNLP was first introduced in 1970 by Richard Brandler and\nJohn Grinder . Grinder , a linguistics expert and Brandler an\nauthor , explored the dimensions of human psychology in\nterms of mind and behavior control.\nThey were some of the first ones to tell humans that it is\npossible to attain more from life by making use of both sides\nof the brain. They are said to have been heavily influenced\nby the work of psychologi sts Virginia Satir, Milton\nErickson and Fritz Perls.\nIn fact, Brandler closely worked  with Perls and Satir to come\nup with the dif ferent ideologies of NLP .\nNLP mainly deals with people capitalizing on their\nbrainpower and doing more by tapping into their complete\nmental capacity .\nI know it sounds a bit complex but it is actually quite easy.\nYou have to first understand the basic concept and then go\nabout exploiting it. Through the course of this book, we will\nlook at how you can do so with ease.\nThrough extens ive study or educated people, Brandler and\nGrinder found that despite having similar educational\nbackgrounds, some people were able to exploit their\neducation and do more in their life whereas some were\nunable to put it to good use and would end up failing at\nfinishing the task at hand.\nThis made them realize that having good education alone\nwas not helping these people succeed and there was\nsomething more that was allowing them to for ge ahead. They\ndecided to investigate and find out what really set these\nsuccessful people apart and what extra they possessed that\nhelped them get to where they were.\nOnce they were done with their research, they were surprised\nto know that the successful people had a different way of\ncommunicating with others, which helped them succeed\nbetter . The ones that were not succeeding as much were not\nable to communicate with others well enough. So, they\ndecided to compile a set of rules that would allow people to\ncommunicate better and thus the concepts of NLP were\nformed.\nWhat sets NLP apart from the rest of the concepts that are\nout there is the fact that it mainl y deals with focusing on the\nsolution as opposed to the problem. Many psychologists\nspend a lot of time listening to a person’ s problems and make\na big deal out of trying to analyze and present these\nproblems. However , NLP will focus on the solution and\ncome up with a feasible one that help the person implement\nit with ease.\nNLP is a concept where people make use of the information\nthat they have and try to apply it practically in the different\nreal life situations that they come across on a daily basis. As\nyou know, everybody is required to take full advantage of\ntheir education and that can be done through the\nimplementation of NLP. Communication is a key aspect and\nNLP teaches people to both communicate internally with\nthemselves and also externally with the outside world.\nThe concept is generally taught by experts who have\nextensive knowledge on the subject. Many schools and\ncolleges now make use of NLP  to teach students and help\nthem understand how they can use their existing knowledge\nand put it to good use.\nProblem solving is one of the main implementations of NLP.\nIt is not limited  to looking at the issue through a single\nviewpoint and deals with analyzing it through several\ndifferent viewpoints before arriving at a feasible solution. It\nis about expanding the horizon s of thought and looking at\nthe bigger picture.\nNow you might be wondering as to who is NLP for? And\nwhether you will be able to take it up and implement it in\nyour life.\nNLP will be beneficial for a whole host of people and there\nis no hard and fast rule that says only certain types of people\ncan take it up. Let us look at who can truly benefit by\nemploying the theories of NLP in their life.\nWorking profes sionals will have the chance to maximize\ntheir career opportunities by making use of NLP. As you\nknow , everybody in the rat race wishes to outdo the other in\norder to be a leader. With the help of NLP, the person will\nknow to make a quick decision and find a solution that will\nhelp solve a problem. He or she will also be able to deal with\neveryday issues with ease thereby increasing their level of\nproductivity .\nStudents can make use of NLP to excel in their studies. NLP\nmainly deals with enhancing internal communication and the\nchild will be able to remember the concepts better , and for a\nlonger period of time. NLP is a simple concept and children\nwill not have to take up rigorou s mental tasks to understand\nand implement it. Parents can start introducing the concept\nto them and they will successfully get their child started on\nit.\nNLP is also for elders. It will help in making their everyday\nlife easy. They will not have to put in too much effort to find\nsolutions to their problems and they can extrapolate and\narrive at quick and feasible solutions to their issues. NLP is a\ntechnique that many elders employ in their day-to-day life,\nas it is quite simple to understand as well.\nRemember that the different problems that you will come\nacross will all have the same thing at their core and you will\nhave to get to it and make use of your common knowledge to\nsolve them.\nMIND CONTROL AND COERCION\nMind control and coercion are two different things. Mind\ncontrol isn’t coercion and it doesn’ t make use of any of the\ntricks or techniques that are made use of in coercion.\nCoercion is the act where the controller wants to have his\nown way, regardless of the feelings, emotions or thoughts of\nthe person whom he is coercing. Threats, humiliation and\neven guilt can be made use of for achieving the end result in\ncoercion. By now you would have understood that there isn’t\nanything positive about coercio n. To coerce an individual\nmeans that you are forcefully making them behave or act in a\ncertain manner that they didn’ t want to and this isn’t what\nmind control is about. In mind  control you don’t force an\nindividual to go against their basic beliefs.\nThe stark difference between coercion and mind control is\nthat coercion doesn’ t understand  the workings of the mind of\nthe person who is being coerce d. Coercion is used by most\nof the cults and leaders for controlling the minds of others. If\nyou have read the Harry Potter books or have seen the\nmovies then you would realize that Lord Voldemort made\nuse of coercion for controlling people by threatening to kill\nor torture them if they don’ t follow him.\nMIND CONTROL AND PERSUASION\nMind control and persuasion  are closely interlinked.\nHowever , they are different from one another . It is important\nthat you understand the difference between these two. For\ngetting a better idea of this concept, take into consideration\nMaslow’ s theory . Every human being has certain needs and\nthese needs can be noted down in the form of a pyramid\naccording to the order of achieving self-actualization.\nPersuasion woul d rest at the bottom of such a pyramid, along\nwith all the other basic needs . On the other hand, mind\ncontrol would be at the top of the pyramid along with self-\nactualization. Persuasion form s the basis for obtaining\ncontrol over the mind.\nAs you keep progressing through higher levels, more control\nand power would be exercised on the mind and when this\npower has reached its maximum, and then you will be able\nto control your mind. A simple example would help you get\na better understanding of this concept. For instance, you\nwant the latest MacBook, but you need your parent’ s or your\nspouse’ s permiss ion for buying it. But when you make use of\nmind control, you will be able to tell yourself that you\ncannot do without that gadget and you will figure out a way\nin which you can acquire it by making it seem acceptable to\nothers.\nYou will need to remember that it is very difficult to control\na person’ s mind and you will need to think beyond the\npresent situation at hand, if you want to really control a\nperson’ s mind. Most of us funct ion with the belief that if we\nreact to a situation in a certain manner , it will help us achieve\nthe outcome that we desire. Therefore, it is safe to say that\nmind control is all about strategic thinking.\nYou will need to think ahead, if you want to achieve the\noutcome you truly desire. This in itself is not an easy task,\nyou will need to understand the manner in which a person\nthinks and also identify the responses that such an individual\nwould give to specific situations. But for doing all this, you\nwill need to have a thorough understanding of yourself. You\nshould be able to control your emotions; impulses and you\nmust be secretiv e about your goals because this is the fastest\nmanner in which you will be able to reach them. In the next\nchapter you will find the different ways in which a person\nthinks and this will help you understand them better .\nWHERE IS MIND CONTROL USED?\nMind control is a process that is used on a daily basis and\nthis section will give you a few examples of mind control\nthat you would encounter in your daily life. The manner in\nwhich you motive your child or other students at school to\nperform better , instilling the belief of God in yourself and\nyour children requires a certain degree of mind control,\ninstill a sense of superiority in a particular group like the\nclassic distinction between the jocks and the nerds, attracting\na person  into a relationship whether it is a professional or a\npersonal relationship, teaching your swim team to display\ncontempt against their competitors, convincing a person to\nbuy a particular product, convincing a policeman to let go of\nyou without getting a ticket for violating any traffic laws and\nconvincing others to give up on their belief and follow your\nbeliefs. I could keep going on and on.\nThe person, who is making use of mind control, clearly\nknows his goals. It is true that when you want something\ntruly, then you will motivate the concerned person to finish\nthe task for you. This is a form of mind control technique\nthat’s made use of in everyd ay life. There are simple\nexamples of mind control all around you. For instance, a\nchild would clean their room because their parents have\nconditioned them since a very young age that it is better to\nhave a clean room. This is a subtle form of mind control.\nMind control is used everywher e and you will need to learn\nto either  accept it or learn how to make use of it yourself.\nObviously it would be a better option to learn it so that you\ncan use it for your own advantage. Mind control is about\ninfluencing a person’ s mindset so that it would be beneficial\nfor you and for doing this you will need to put in some\neffort. During the time of elect ions, we see a lot of people\nwho are trying to do this. The political leaders, in a bid to get\nyour votes, they give speeches that address various issues\nand this is actually a method of mind control. The speeches\nthat they give are designed and written in such a way that\nthey would get them the maximum possible votes. The party\nknows that in areas where the number of votes they are\ngoing to get is low, then in such areas the speeches are\nwritten so that they could motivate and encourage people to\nvote for them. The advertisements on television also make\nuse of the same technique. The advertisements that we see\nwill leave an impression on our subconscious mind and\nthat’s why we tend to retain what we see. For instance, if an\nadvert says that cutting down on salt would be good for\nhealth, chances are that we will not only start practicing that\nunconsciously but we will also pass on the same message to\nothers as well.\nThe main problem with mind control is that it is not just\nabout positive things; it can even lead you to believe things\nthat aren’ t as simple as we thought they were when portrayed\nin the advertis ements. For instance, all the cosmetic\ncompanies keep coming up with new ingredients that they\nkeep adding to their products that pretty much baffle the\naudience. If you watch an advertisement for a cosmetic\nproduct the next time, you will notice that the advertisers\ndesign the advertisement in such a way that it gives the\nimpression to the viewers as if they are learning something\nnew and the viewers will definitely remember what they\n“learned” from the advert and end up buying the product.\nThe point here is that, subliminal messages are capable of\nchanging people’ s mindset in a very subtle way .\nMind control is about understanding the mindset of others\nand adjusting the tasks in such a manner that it would give a\npositive feedback. Follow this book to learn more about\nmind control.\n \nCHAPTER 2 \nHOW PEOPLE THINK\nPeople can generally be categorized into three broad\ncategories based  on the manner  of their thinking and these\nare as follows.\nSERIAL THINKING\nHumans are all programmed to react in different manner to\ndifferent situations. The intensity of the reaction varies from\none person to another and this reaction is without any\nconscious thought. This method ensures that we don't think\nabout it. This kind of thinki ng has been associated to\nlemmings walki ng over a cliff top. Serial thinkers are the\nones who will follow the mass es regardless of whether the\ndirection the masses are headed in was safe or not.\nLINEAR THINKING\nLinear thinking is very different from serial thinking. In\nserial thinking there is no conscious thought process that\ntakes place, whereas in linear thinking there's a lot of thought\nthat goes into it. It not only involves the ability to understand\nand predict the probable outcomes of the actions you do, but\nit also makes you think about the most efficient course of\naction that can be adopted for meeting the goal. For getting a\nbetter understan ding of this concept, think of it as a game of\nchess where you not only have to think about the move you\nare making but also analyze the move to understand the\nlikely moves your opponent could make. So, it is about\nanalyzing a situation, thinking about the pros and cons of\neach situation and predicting the likely outcome in a logical\nmanner . Linear thinking is easy to deal with when you are\nworking on mind control becau se you are able to anticipate\nthat the subject matter will have to go through a detailed\nanalysis of the minute details that would eventually lead to\nthe desired conclusion. If you can manage to tap into these\nthoughts, you will definitely be able to change them to play\nin your favor .\nNON – LINEAR THINKING\nNon-linear think ing is a step above linear thinking. It can\neven incorporate the dimensions of time and space. If you\nhave watched the movie Sherlock Holmes in the movie\nGame of Shado ws, this is a classic example of non-linear\nthinking. He analyses every move that he wants to make and\nat the same time also analyses the ways in which he can play\nthe game better while understanding the moves that would\nbe beneficial for him. At the end of the movie he even\nmanages to stages his own death so that he can catch the bag\nguys red-hande d. He portrays what a non-linear thinking\nman would be like. These thinkers, they think outside the\nbox but their intuition always guides them. They notice\nthings that are seldom noticed by others and this makes their\npoint of view much different from the rest. Such individuals\nwill prove to be difficult subjects to exercise mind control\nover but it is possible if you can mange to understand their\nmindset and lay traps that would lead them to the conclusion\nthat you want them to reach. There was a non-linear thinker\nin the character Patrick Jane from a popular TV series, The\nMentalist, he was capable of reading people and often\nnoticed things that others didn't see. This ability is there\nwithin every single one of us, but not many make use of it\nand that is the only difference between non-linear thinkers\nand the rest.\nETHICS OF MIND CONTROL\nLike every other discipline, even this area of study has\ncertain ethics that need to be followed while practicing it. Of\ncourse, these ethics aren't hard and fast rules. There are\nnumerous people all over the world who have made use of\nmind control techniques for achieving their goals and\ndreams. Some people are extre mely good  at this and can\nmake other individuals feel that what they are doing is\nbeneficial for them. Then there are some who haven't got any\nskills in this regard and their actions can have dire\nconsequences. Therefore, it's advisable that you make use of\nthese practices on people whom you are comfortable with. If\nyou don't find the practices of mind control an annoyance\nwhen they are used on you, then you can go ahead a day use\nthem on others. There's another thing that you should keep in\nyour mind and it's that you shouldn't make use of money\ncontrol when you are angry , hurt or are extremely emotional,\nbecause you wouldn't be in a situation to understand or\nworry about the consequences of your actions on others.\nEmotions tend to get in the way of logic and your actions\ncould hurt those on whom you were performing mind\ncontrol. Howeve r, you need to be mindful of the fact that\nthose people could hurt you in a manner similar to the one\nthat you tried hurting them in. Negative thoughts are copse\nof altering the thought process and the individual wouldn't\nbe able to think  in a coherent manner that's consistent with\nlinear thinking. Those who make use of mind control in a\nnegative manner are those individuals who seek to have\npower over someone else. The mentally abided housewife\nwould put up with her husband and control her because she\nis in a very fragile psychological state. The abuser would\nmake use of this to further weaken his partner . This is an\nexample of improper use of mind control.\nYou might want to inform your friends about the knowledge\nthat you possess on mind control. My sincere request would\nbe that you refra in from doing that. You wouldn’ t want your\ndear ones to start thinking that any change in their behavior\nis due to your influence on them. Instead it would be better\nto let them realize all this on their own without your\ninterference. There is another thing that you should do; you\nneed to ask yourself why it is important to read someone’ s\nmind for you. If your answer is that you want to obtain a\ngreater understanding of how the human mind reasons, then\nyou have got a very good reason and sufficient motive to go\nahead with it. But, if you are making use of mind control for\nany negative reasons, then you shouldn’ t use mind control\nbecause it would amount to coercion if you want to force\nsomeone to do or abstain from doing an act that isn’t in sync\nwith their well being and is against their will. Human beings\nare blessed with intelligence so that they could help in\nmaking things better for themselves and those who are\naround them and its intention isn’t to make someone else’s\nlife worse. Therefore, when you are using mind control,\nplease make sure that you are doing it for the right reasons.\nTYPES OF PEOPLE\nYou will need to remember that there are two types of people\nwhen it comes to using mind control. There are some people\nwho are controlled by their emotions and then there are\nothers who are purely controlled by their survival instincts.\nThe reason for this distinction is obvious. Women tend to be\nmore emotional and men like to feel that they are in control\nbut not necessa rily in an emotional way. A man would\nrespond more effectively to something that makes him feel\nlike he would become an effective provider and a woman\nwould expect whatever mind control that can be exercised to\nfall within her emotional beliefs. This makes woman\ndifficult subjects to perform mind control on because there\nisn’t any clear logical thinkin g. Men tend to be linear\nthinkers and women tend to think by weighing in their\nemotions. \nYou will need to keep this in mind when you are exercising\nmind control. Have you ever been stopped for going over the\nspeeding limit? Then you would clearly remember the cop\ncoming over and informing you that you will get a ticket for\nspeeding. You can make use of mind control in such a\nsituation. You will need to understand that the way the cop\nreacts to you depends upon the way you respond to him. At\nthe risk of sounding sexist, male cops tend to be fairly easy\nto predict. They have a job that they have to do and they do\nit well indeed, but it wouldn’ t hurt if you could bend the\nrules a little for your own convenience, would it? I guess not.\nYou will need to be humble, apologetic, cooperative and\nsmile a lot so that you can make them feel comfortable and\nonce you have managed to do this, then chances are that you\nwouldn’ t be given a ticket and would probably be let go with\njust a warning.\nIf you are a wom an, then you can try and see the results for\nyourself the next time you get pulled over. But, if you try the\nsame technique on a female cop, then don’ t hold your breath;\nyou are just wasting your time. The answer to this question\nis very simple, they already are of the mindset that men have\nan unfai r advantage and in order to prove that they are more\nefficient workers, they will not be swayed by your charm.\nYou cannot say with 100% certainty that men and women\nrespond dif ferently . You can, however just try and predict the\nlikely outcome in each situation. Women respond to\nsituations in their professional and personal life quite\ndifferently . So, don’t count on them behaving in the same\nmanner everywhere.\n \nCHAPTER 3 \nELEMENTS OF NLP\nAs you know , there are three core concepts in NLP namely -\nNeuro, linguistic and programm ing. You have to understand\neach of these individually in order to exploit the subject\nsuccessfully .\nNEURO\nNeuro stands for anything that is related to the brain. I’m\nsure you have heard of the concept of neurology , which\nstands for understanding everything that the brain does.\nIn a day, our senses work towards helping us in picking up\nthe different stimulus that surrounds us. Right from odors to\nsight and sounds to smells and also textures, our senses relay\na message to our brains, which then interprets it and\ngenerates an appropriate response.\nThe mind is divided into two sections namely the conscious\nmind and the subconscious mind. The former is what you\nwill use to make everyday decisions and what your senses\nare all connecte d to. The latter is what will automatically\nkick into action without you having to instruct your brain.\nThe latter makes our life extrem ely easy as we do not have\nto put in too much thought into carrying out certain everyday\nactivities. However , we will still have to consult our\nconscious mind for a lot of everyday decisions, which can\nseem a bit cumbersome.\nBut what if you were able to take away some of that load\nfrom your conscious mind? What if a lot more decisions\nwere automatically implemented by your subconscious\nmind? W ill that not make your life a lot easier?\nSurely it would! And to help you attain the same, you can\nmake use of NLP. NLP will help your conscious and\nsubconscious minds conver ge. You will be able to do more\nautomatically and will not have to rely on your conscious\nmind as much. Decision-making will get easy and\nimplementation will get easier .\nYour mind will be able to relate  to things that are similar in\nnature and respond faster . It will be like collecting all the\ninformation that lies in your brain and sending it into\nspecific folders that will keep the information safe for a long\ntime. All that you will do is extrapolate the information and\napply it to the dif ferent situations that will arise in your life.\nLINGUISTIC\nThe next concept in NLP is that of linguistics. Linguistics\nstands for the study of languages. When it comes to\ncommunication, it is obvious that your language has to be up\nto the mark and simple for others to understand. If others do\nnot understand what you are saying or you don’t get what\nthey are telling you, then how will you progress? Language\nbarriers can seem quite annoying, especially if they are\ninternal in nature. Human beings are some of the most\nexpressive creat ures on earth and it would be a shame if we\nare unable to express our thoughts and feelings effectively .\nSo, we have to improve on how we speak with others and\ndrive our point across. We should put in efforts to establish a\nlanguage that is universal and will help us communicate\nbetter .\nAt the same time, you must also be adept at internal\ncommunication, in order to know what exactly your mind is\nthinking. Interna l communication is of vital importance and\nyou should try to be as clear about things to yourself as\npossible to take quick action. If your mind is saying one\nthing and you are doing another  thing, then it will not work\nin your favor . The idea is to come up with a language that\nwill make it easy for you to interpret what you are thinking\nand how best it can be implemented.\nPROGRAMMING\nThe third conce pt is known as programming. As you know ,\nprogramming refers to bifurcating the information and\nsending it to the different folde rs in the brain. You program\nyourself to think a certain way in order to make the most of\nyour time and knowledge.\nWhen we are young, our minds are fresh and able to capture\nmany aspects of life. We are able to also easily dissipate the\ninformation and remember things for a long time. However ,\nwith age, that aspect of our mind changes and we find it\ndifficult to process and keep safe the information. We find\nourselves to be in need of help and that help will be provided\nto us by NLP .\nNLP will teach us to not just acquire and divide the\ninformation but also send it to the different parts of the brain,\nfrom where it will be quite easy for it to recall the\ninformation.\nOnce you understand these core concepts, you will be able to\ntake up NLP on a regular basis.\nYou have to understand that NLP is goal oriented. So, unless\nyou attain the goal that you set out to achieve, your mind\nwill not rest. You will have to put in the appropriate efforts\ntowards attaining the end result.\nYou must also know that NLP will try to bring about a\nchange in your current style of thinking and you should be\nprepared for it. NLP will help you comprehend things in a\ndifferent way and also teach you to implement the solutions\nin the best possi ble manner . If you remain rigid then you will\nnot see the desired changes.\nYou have to embrace the concept with an open mind and be\nprepared to learn new things. You will find it easy to\nincorporate NLP in your life if you tell your mind to focus\non the task at hand, no matter how small or big it is.\n \n \nCHAPTER 4 \nPREDETERMINED ELEMENTS OF NLP\nBy now you have understood what NLP is all about and\nwhat its individual concepts stand for .\nLet us now look at basic elements of NLP that manifest its\ntrue meaning.\nPERCEPTION\nNLP lays a lot of emphasis on perception. As you know , our\nminds work in a complex manner . We might not fully\nunderstand how we perceive things and all we know is that\nindividual perceptions differ. NLP states that our\nunderstanding of this world is not based on what exists, but\nrather how we look at it. So, although successful people and\nnon-successful people look at the same things before\nforming an opinion, the former use their power of judgement\nto analyze it successfully . That is what gives them the chance\nto take the right decisions. So it is really not about what\nexists in this world but rather our perception of it.\nSUCCESS LIES WITHIN YOU\nThis is another important element of NLP that you should\nunderstand in order to implem ent it in your life. As you\nknow , everybody has an inner strength that allows them to\nportray a strong image of themselves. When it comes to\nNLP, it teaches people that perception lies inwards and so\ndoes potential. If you keep looking outward to find a way to\nattain success, then you will not find it. You have to look\ninternally to find something that will help you in your quest\nto attain success. The founders of NLP found that successful\npeople were able to tap into their full potential and would\nimplement the needful to interpret the opportunity and make\nthe most of it.\nRESPECT OTHERS\nAs was mentioned earlier , everybody in this world has their\nown unique sense of perception. Y ou will not be the only one\nwith a view and there will be others that will look at the\nsame things as you. It is not possible for them to think just as\nyou do and so, you will have to accept their viewpoint.\nEmpathy is a big thing in NLP. You will have to think from\nanother person’ s point of view while trying to find solutions\nto problems. Mocking or questioning others will only pull\nyou down and not allow you to progress.\nMAKE CONNECTIONS\nNLP states that it is extremely important for people to make\ndue connections  in respect to perception. This means that it\nis important to understand how others perceive and respond\nto things. It means that people’ s words and thoughts are\ninterconnected and not independent. You have to carefully\nlisten to what people are saying to get an insight into what\nthey are trying to say. Based on it, you will know what\nexactly is going on in their mind. Even if you think you are\nnot going to be affected by what others have to say, you will\nhave to carefully evaluate it and form your own perception.\nKNOW HOW T O CONNECT\nIn the previous segment we understood that it is important to\nconnect people’ s words to their thoughts. However , that does\nnot mean you judge people through their behavior . Many\ntimes people end up behaving a certain way , which might not\nbe relevant to how they think. Some people might behave in\na difficult manner but that migh t not be in their true nature.\nYou will have to judge them based on their entire personality\nand accept them for who they are.\nOPTIONS\nNLP encourages  you to have several options ready in order\nto make the right decision. This means that you have to pick\nthe best from many options and not have just one plan of\naction. These options refer to solutions to the problems that\nyou are trying to solve. You will obviously have to have\nalternates and it will only get easy for you if you have two or\nthree back up plans in place, and you can freely fall on them.\nNO F AILURE\nNLP does not believe in the concept of failure. You have to\nunderstand that although sometimes you think you have\nfailed, it’s only about the system having rejected your\nsolution. So you must not feel disheartened and instead\nmove to the next feasible solution. As was mentioned earlier ,\nyou have to have certain option s ready , which will help you\nhave back up plans.\nThese form the dif ferent predetermined concepts of NLP .\n \n \nCHAPTER 5 \nIMPLEMENTING NLP IN \nYOUR LIFE\nIn order  to incorporate NLP in your life, you will have to\nfollow a few steps. The steps to adopt are as follows.\nOBSER VE\nStart by observing your current  behavior . Look at how you\nrespond to the different stimuli that surround you. How well\ndo you communicate with others? How do you perceive the\nthings around you? What do you think is people’ s opinion of\nyou? You have to find an answer to all these questions and\nwrite them down. You will be referring back to them later\nwhile evaluating your progress.\nCOMP ARE\nThe next step is to get others to observe you and your\nbehavior . As was mentioned earlier , not everybody thinks\nalike and there will always be a difference in opinion. You\nhave to ask someone at home, and your colleague or friend\nat office to write down snippets of your behavior . Collect\ntheir response and compare it with what you have written\ndown. That will help you know  if you are really acting the\nway you think you are or it is much different from other\npeople’ s perception of you.\nSET GOALS\nNext, set yourself some reasonable goals that you can\npursue. These goals should help you communicate better ,\nlisten better, present your views in a better way etc. All of it\nwill come together to help you become an all-round better\nperson.\nTAKE ACTION\nNext, you must devise a plan of action that will help you\nattain the set goals. Taking action might be the most\nimportant step here as it is quite easy to make plans but\ntaking action is what is usually tough to do. You have to see\nwhere you are going wrong and fix the issue. At the same\ntime, if you are getting something right then you must stick\nwith it. For example, if you are good at starting\nconversations then you must enhance the habit by learning to\npursue the conversation in a better way. On the other hand, if\nyou are a bad listener , then you have to develop the habit of\nlistening carefully .\nEVALUA TE\nOnce you start pursuing your goals, you must evaluate from\ntime to time to see if you are on track. You must have your\nplan of action on the one hand and measure your progress on\nthe other. You must check if you are consciously making\nefforts to change yourself and embracing the change with\nopen arms.\nOnce you think you have achieved what you set out to\nachieve, you can move to another goal and so on.\n \n \nCHAPTER 6 \nWHERE YOU SHOULD USE NLP\nNLP finds many uses in different fields of life. In this\nchapter , we will look at the different places where you can\nemploy the concepts of NLP . \nPERSONAL LIFE\nCommunication\nCommunication with family members is extremely\nimportant. It will help you emote your feelings properly and\nyou will not have to hold on to them. You will also be able to\navoid unnecessa ry fights at home and avail a peace of mind.\nCommunication will also bring you closer together as a\nfamily and will help you lead a better life. This is especially\nimportant in this day and age where people fail to understand\nthe value of having and maintaining relationships.\nValue yourself\nNLP will teach you to value yourself. As you know ,\nperception plays a big part in how you respond to things\naround you and generally , it is observed that people go bit\nharsh on themselves. But you have to love yourself in order\nto attain success. You must accept your thought process and\nevaluate it. Don’ t beat yourself up for the negative aspects,\nyou can work on them and change them. You must make\nyour positive attributes the hero and pursue it.\nPositive change\nNLP will bring about an overa ll positive change. You and\nyour family members will be able to attain your goals and\nlead a great life. The creation of ideal relationships will help\nyou stave off unnecessary stress and tensions. The rapport\nthat you build with each other will go a long way in helping\nyou develop self-confidence. You will always know that\nyour family will back you no matter what the circumstances\nand that will give you the confidence to attain the best in life.\nPROFESSIONAL LIFE\nProfessionally , you can attain a lot of benefits by\nimplementing NLP .\nProblem solving\nSolving problems at work is one of the most important tasks\nand if you rise up and shine then you will surely get noticed.\nYou might be able to impress your boss and get a promotion!\nBut before that, you have to implement NLP and know how\nto solve problems effectively . As you know , communication\nis extremely important and you will have to communicate\nwith your colleagues and co-w orkers and listen to all their\nfeedback before deciding upon a resolution.\nManage\nWith NLP, you will find it easy to manage the different\npeople in your office. People management can sometimes\nseem like cumbersome task, it is especially important if there\nare a lot of people in your office and you have the\nresponsibility to have all of them on the same page. NLP\nwill teach you to be patient and lead the way. You will find it\nrather easy to get everybody to listen to what you have to\nsay. Again, your management skills might help you climb\nthe ladder .\nLeadership\nLeadership skills are important, especially if you wish to see\nyour company progress. Lead ing professionals is much\nharder than leading children. You have to keep everybody\nhappy and listen to what each one has to say. Patience is\nimportant and also the ability to control the crowd. Through\nthe implementation of NLP, you will be able to do all of it\nwith much ease. As was mentioned earlier , successful people\nwill know to implement an actio n at the right time and make\nthe most of their abilities. That is what will help make the\nleader stronger .\nSales\nDriving up sales is important for any company but it is easier\nsaid than done. You have to work on finding the best\nproducts or services that is bringing in the most business.\nSales numbers can be increased by communicating better\nwith your team.  You have to make it a point to go through\nyour company’ s history to see what has worked and repeat\nthe same to have a winning streak.\nCustomer service\nCustomers are possibly the most important aspects of a\ncompany . You need to keep your customers happy if you\nwish to sustain your company . For that, you must establish a\nclear line of communication with them. NLP, as you know ,\nwill help you speak freely and clearly thereby reaching out\nto your audience. You will be able to solve their issues faster\nthereby making them happy .\nThese are just some of the ways in which NLP will help your\nprofessionally but you must note that it is not limited to just\nthese. As and when you implement NLP, you will be\nacquainted with the other benefits of NLP .\nSOCIAL LIFE\nNLP can be used to impact your social life as well. Here is\nhow.\nNETWORKING\nThe more you network, the better your life gets. You must\nnot limit yourself to just the people you currently know . You\nhave to reach out and make as many new friends as possible.\nYou never know  when one of them will prove to be a great\naddition to your friend circle and help you avail more out of\nyour life. NLP will help you make new friends and also hold\non to the ones you already have.\nSOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY\nNLP will help you increase your social responsibility . As\nyou know, it is important for you to give back to the society .\nYou can contribute in any which way you like as long as you\nthink it will help you establish a positive impact. Some ideas\ninclude hosting health camps or organizing a day of fun and\ngames for children etc. You will have the chance to organize\nsomething on a large scale, which will improve your\ncapacity to undertake lar ge projects. \nAgain, it is not limited to just these benefits. You will know\nabout the many other uses of NLP as and when you take it\nup.\n \n \nCHAPTER 7 \nNLP AND HYPNOSIS\nWe looked at how you can implement NLP in your life and\nnow; we will see how you can use it to influence others.\nHuman beings have the capacity to get others to listen to\nthem. It might sound a bit tough to do but is highly possible.\nYou will have to know how to go about it and you will\nsurely be able to influence others to listen to you and do as\nyou say .\nIn this chapter , we will look at some of the things that you\ncan do to effectively influence people and hypnotize them to\ndo as you say .\nAPPROACH\nThe first thing is to approach the person that you wish to\ninfluence. The person has to be someone that you think will\ndefinitely listen  to you and take your command. The best\nthing is to try and influence someone that has already been\ninfluenced by you and is taken aback by your charm. You\nwill surely have someone of the nature in your office or\nfriend circle. Once you know who it will be, you should\napproach them the right way. Call them to you and stand\nstraight in front of them. You should be at your charming\nbest and be as presentable as possible.\nTRANCE\nNext, you have to say things that will cause the person to get\nlost in what you have to say. You have to pick your words\ncarefully and ensure that they are engrossed in it. You have\nto try and get them to read your lips. Don’ t go straight to the\npoint. Discuss something before giving them the\ninstructions.\nSPEAK\nNext, give them the instruction so that they clearly\nunderstand it. You have to keep  it simple and to the point.\nFor example, if you want them to do something within a\nspecific period of time, tell them clearly what you are\nexpecting from them. You must also tell them that you are\nresting a lot of hope on them as that will trigger off a sense\nof responsibility in them. You have to get them to repeat\nwhat you told them to ensure that they have understood it\ncorrectly .\nTONE/ PITCH\nYou have to know what sort of pitch and tone to use when\nyou are trying to influence someone. If you are trying to\ngenerate excitem ent, then you should speak in a high pitch.\nAnd if you are trying to estab lish responsibility then you\nshould use a low pitch. You must also make use of the right\ntone to drive the point across as best as you can.\nSNAP\nNext, you should snap your finger to help them come out of\nthe trance. I know it sounds a bit too bookish but you might\nhave to do so to help the person snap back to normalcy . It\nwill also signal them to go straight to the task that you have\ngiven them. You can also do something milder like brush\nyour shoulder or some such sign that helps break their\nconcentration.\nREPEA T\nOnce you find the right person  to influence, you have to\nkeep it going with them. Only then will you be able to get\nbetter at it. Repeating your actions will also help you\ndevelop the confidence and move to another person that you\ncan influence.\n \n \nCHAPTER 8 \nSOME MIND \nCONTROL TECHNIQUES\nBeing a leader is not an easy job. It is quite difficult for\nleaders to control employees and yet is one of the most\nactivities that need to be undertaken at the of fice.\nIn this chapter , we will look at a few mind-controlling\ntechniques that will make it easy for a leader to control a\ngroup of people.\nREW ARD/ PUNISHMENT SYSTEM\nThe first type of mind control technique is the reward and\npunishment system. It is quite easy to understand and you\nwill be able to control your entire gamut of employees by\nimplementing the system.\nIt calls for you to announce to your employees that\nwhosoever performs the best will be awarded and whoever\ndoes the worst will be punished.\nThis is a simple  system but very effective. The employees\nwill try to do their best and establish healthy competition.\nYou must keep an eye on your employees and find the best\nones. You must also pick out the least productive employees\nand list them.\nYou will have to reward the first few and punish the last few.\nRemember that the reward has to be really worthwhile and\nwhat your employees will appreciate.\nOn the other hand, the punishment should not be too harsh. It\nshould be some thing like staying behind half an hour extra\nevery day after work or some such punishment.\nYou have to try and pick a different winner each time and\nalso a different person to punis h. Rewarding the same one\nand punishing the same employee might make the latter feel\npushed and bad.\nRemember that they should not know your intentions of\ntrying to control them by announcing these schemes. They\nmust assume that you are doing it to better the company .\nSome people take a unique approach where one week they\nwill reward a particular type of action and the following\nweek they will punish it. This is generally done to prevent\npeople from continuing the same type of actions for long. By\ncreating a confusing environment, they will be able to\ncontrol the thoughts and actions of the dif ferent individuals.\nA similar technique can be employed at home as well, to\ncontrol your family members or children. You must\nannounce rewards for all those that are doing their bit at\nhome and punish those that are not doing their work\nproperly . For example, you should award them if they are\ncleaning their room regularly and also maintaining the house\nwell and punish them if they are littering.\nOnce they are punished, they will learn their lesson and not\nrepeat it. You can also punish your children if they are not\ndoing their homework and reward them if they are doing\ntheir homework properly .\nSo this system of reward and punishment will work\nuniversally . You can use it anyw here that you wish to control\nothers.\nREACTION TECHNIQUE\nThe next technique is known as the reaction technique. It is\none where you praise the worker in order to get the best out\nof them. Reaction technique is just as effective as the\nprevious one. It is one where you will be able to positively\ninfluence the other person. You don’t have to rely on a\nreward or punish ment system for it. All you have to do is tell\nthem that you have rested a lot of faith in them and you\nconsider them the best employee in the company . This will\nencourage them to put in their best.\nThese form the two mind control models that you can\nemploy to control your workers’ minds.\n \nCHAPTER 9 \nSOME MORE TECHNIQUES OF MIND\nCONTROL\nThere are different techniques that can be made use of for\ncontrolling one’s emotions, actions as well as thoughts. The\ntechniques that are mentioned in this chapter should help you\nin controlling others minds without much trouble. These\ntechniques will only provide a certain degree of compliance.\nIn this chapter we will take a look at the most common\nmodels of mind control that are used.\nTHE BEHA VIORAL CONDITIONING MODEL\nA person practicing mind control would generally make sure\nthat his objectives and goals are achieved. He would make\nsure that the people whom he is trying to control would do\nwhat he wants them to do and do so willingly . He would\nmake sure that the people are under the impression that they\nare perfo rming a certain action or task because they want to\nand not because  they are being made to do it. For instance,\nlet us consider a situation here you have a puppy at home.\nThis puppy will need to be trained and for doing so, you\nwould give the puppy a treat when he does something you\napprove of and punish him when ", "metadata": {"category": "mkultra_benchmark", "topic": "mind_control_research"}}
