feit  our values and\ncharacter  as a moral leader  to justify  short term advantages  in intelligence\ngathering.  If the great United  States sets an example  of not abiding  by\ntreaties  and international  law, no other countries  will. The long term soft\npower  of the United  States will be mitigated  forever.\nThis book tries to find the balance  of the harsh, unbridled  truth\nwith its interviews  and sensitivity  to readers  who may get nightmares\nfrom them. Anyone  who buys this book to read generally  is not afraid of\ntruth and values  truth no matter  what predetermined  emotional\nassociations  they have.\n\nIntroduction\nThere have been several cataclysmic  knowledge  events in human\nhistory that have changed the world view of the collective  understanding:\nfire for cavemen,  Earth is ellipsoidal,  stars are suns, and DNA is the\ngenetic biological  program for examples.  Now we enter the boundary  in\nhuman understanding  of where the mind and neuroscience  intersect,  the\nsubjective  and objective  perceptions  of realities overlap.\nThis field of study is often called psychophysics,\nneuropsychology,  or cybernetics.  \"Cybernetics\"  comes from a Greek\nword meaning  \"the art of steering”. Cybernetics  is about having a goal\nand taking action to achieve that goal. Knowing  whether  you have\nreached your goal (or at least are getting closer to it) requires \"feedback\",\na concept that comes from cybernetics. From the Greek, \"cybernetics\"\nevolved  into Latin as \"governor\".\nCybernetics  as a process operating  in nature has been around for a\nlong time. Cybernetics  as a concept in society has been around at least\nsince Plato used it to refer to government. In modern times, the term\nbecame widespread  because  Norbert Wiener wrote a book called ,\n\"Cybernetics\"  in 1948, a year after the formation  of the CIA. His sub-title\nwas \"control and communication  in the animal and machine\".  This was\nimportant  because it connects control (a.k.a., actions taken in hope of ;\nachieving  goals) with communication  (a.k.a., connection  and information\nflow between  the actor and the environment).  So, Wiener is pointing  out\nthat effective  action requires communication.\nWiener's sub-title also states that both animals (biological\nsystems) and machines  (non-biological  or \"artificial\"  systems)  can\noperate according  to cybernetic  principles.  This was an explicit\nrecognition  that both living and non-living  systems can have purpose. A\nscary idea in 1948.!\nBrave New world\nee\n' \"Getting  Started\" Guide to Cybernetics,  Pangaro,\nhitp://www.pangaro.com/published/eyber-macmillan.  htmlIntroduction\nBy Nathan  Cochrane\nJuly 23 2002\nNext\nA draft government  report says we will alter human evolution\nwithin 20 years by combining  what we know of nanotechnology,\nbiotechnology,  IT and cognitive  sciences.  The 405-page  report sponsored\nby the US National  Science  Foundation  and Commerce  Department,\nConverging  Technologies  for Improving  Human Performance,  calls for a\nbroad-based  research  program  to improve  human performance  leading to\ntelepathy,  machine-to-human  communication,  amplified  personal  sensory\ndevices  and enhanced  intellectual  capacity.\nPeople may download  their consciousnesses  into computers  or\nother bodies even on the other side of the solar system, or participate  in a\ngiant \"hive mind\", a network  of intelligences  connected  through  ultra-fast\ncommunications  networks.  \"With knowledge  no longer encapsulated  in\nindividuals,  the distinction  between  individuals  and the entirety of\nhumanity  would blur,\" the report says. \"Think Vulcan mind-meld.  We\nwould perhaps  become  more of a hive mind - an enormous,  single,\nintelligent  entity.\"\nArmies may one day be fielded by machines  that think for\nthemselves  while devices will respond  to soldiers' commands  before their\nthoughts  are fully formed, it says. The report says the abilities  are within\nour grasp but will require an intense public-relations  effort to \"prepare\nkey organisations  and societal activities  for the changes  made possible  by\nconverging  technologies\",  and to counter  concern  over \"ethical,  legal and\nmoral\" issues. Education  should be overhauled  down to the primary-\nschool level to bridge curriculum  gaps between  disparate  subject areas.\nProfessional  societies  should be open to practitioners  from other\nfields, it says. \"The success of this convergent-technologies  priority  area\nis crucial to the future of humanity,\"  the report says.\nwtec.org/ConvergingTechnologies/Report/NBIC-pre-publi  tion.pdf\n\nto discuss devices that \"make selected adversaries  think or act according\nto our needs... By studying  and modeling  the human brain and nervous\nsystem, the ability to mentally  influence  or confuse personnel  is also\npossible.\"\nThe American  military  may want to attack the nervous system,\nwith pain rays and laser plasma pulses. But they're not the only ones. The\nRussians  have long studied such systems,  too -- including  one weapon\nthat could, in theory, remotely  trigger heart attacks.\nIn 2003, at the 2nd European  Symposium  on Non-Lethal\nWeapons,  Anatoly Korolev  and his colleagues  from Moscow  State University\npresented  a paper with the snappy title \"Bioelectrodynamic  Criterion  of\nthe NLW Effectiveness  Estimation  and the Interaction  mechanisms  of the\nmultilayer  Skin Tissues  with electromagnetic  Radiation.\"  This is a study\nof how radio-frequency  weapons  -- like the American  Active Denial\nSystem -- affect the skin. After wading  through  a mass of technical  data\nshowing  how complex  the interactions  are we reach the punch line:\nThe sensations  modality  (pricking,  touch, pressure,  gooseflesh,\nburning,  pain etc) depends  on the field  parameters  and individual\nconcrete  human being  factors. As a matter of fact, we can really choose\nthe non-lethal  bioeffect.\nThe effects include sensations  similar to those discussed\npreviously,  and more besides. The paper discusses  effects on cell\nmembranes  and affecting  the body’s normal function,  including  \"information\ntransfer  to the organs of control.\"\n‘At the same conference,  V Makukhin  of the Trymas Engineering\nCenter in Moscow  described  \"Electronic  equipment  for complex\ninfluence  on biological  objects.\"  And when he says \"biological  objects,\"\nhe means you and me.\nHis laboratory  apparatus  uses a modulated  beam of radio waves to\nproduce  what he terms \"disorder  of autonomic  nervous system,\"  put\nforward  as a possible  non-lethal  weapon. Makhunin  notes that there is no\ngeneral agreement  on how EM waves disrupt nerves - he mentions  ion\nchannels similar to those in the plasma paper - but he certainly  seems to be\nseeing the same effects as American  researchers.\nBut it need not be a non-lethal  weapon. Makukhin  also mentions\nthe effects of \"change  of electrocardiogram\"  and what he calls \"functionIntroduction\nbreak of heart muscle.\"\nThe vulnerability  of the heart to electrical  stimulation  (including\nthat produced  by EM waves) is well documented.  A lethal device would\ninterfere  with the electrical  potentials  that keep the chambers  of the heart\nsynchronized,  producing  fibrillation  and rapid death. A death ray doesn’t\nneed to be a truck-sized  laser that reduces  the target to smoking  heap; a\nsmall device  that stops the heart will do the job.\n: Little has been openly  published  in this area in the public domain,\nbut this may be the tip of the iceberg.  We are likely to be hearing  more in\nfuture - especially  if the Russians  manage  to find funding.\nI don’t think we need tinfoil hats just yet. But a layer of\nconducting  mesh built into body armor might save a lot of heartache  in\nyears to come.\n-- David Hambling,  Weapons  Grade, Carroll  & Graf, 2005.\n\nInformation,  psychological,  cybernetic,  neurological,  sociological,\ncultural,  economic  warfare  and all other kinds of social engineering  has\nits exact equivalent  in computer  science  models.  This is not coincidental.\nBiological  intelligence  was evolution’s  design  of computing.  There is a\nlarge push in the defense  department  as of the writing  of this book to\nstudy computer  hacking  and cyber warfare.  While  this is a real threat, it is\nalso a cover  story. Every computer  hacking  technique  is applicable  to\nhumans  and human  networks.  It gives the organizations  new ideas of how\nto control  and “protect”  society  and its culture.  This is why they run\noffensive  information  war games,  which aren’t  games  at all to the\ninnocent  people  that get included.\nTopics  and Take-a-ways  from this chapter:\n1. Understanding  that the historical,  political  and military  pursuit  of\ncontrolling  human  beings,  interrogating  them, and persuading  populations\nthrough  devious  means is not a new agenda.\n2\" Brains are just biological  computers  and the data from the senses\nare input and output  ports. The mind is the software  or neural network\ndesign  of how the data is processed.\n38 The information  warfare,  psychological  warfare,  perception\nwarfare,  cognitive  warfare,  and communication  warfare  units use\ncomputer  science  models  when hacking  into minds  and reprogramming\ntheir fundamental  algorithms  thereby  altering  behavior  and perception.\n4. Many  of the detailed  models,  methods,  and tactics  of hacking\ncomputer  systems  and their equivalence  of hacking  human  beings  and\norganizations  are inseparable  and have been integrated  into one complete\nsystem.\n\n2|Page Project: Soul Catcher\nHistory of Mind Hacking\nEven before computers,  sharing brain signals was being done. In\nits simplest  form, quasi-static  high voltage fields were used to read the\nEEG from one person ,amplify the signal, and modulate  a high voltage\nfield on another and vice versa. It has been spoofed in cartoons since\n1960s as mad science fiction. The feedback  in both directions  is\nextremely  important  to accomplish  this feat. Often this technology  has\nbeen spoofed in science fiction movies by showing  a scientist swapping\nconsciousnesses  with two people using these high voltage helmets that\ndon’t actual touch the skin but the capacitive  effect causes small currents\nin the brain. Movies are used to acclimate  the next generation  that this\ntechnology  is being done and they should accept it when it is finally\nrevealed  to them. The technology  is amazing  but it doesn’t happen\ninstantly  like in the movies  nor is it perfect.\nThe human brain has two hemispheres  grossly identical  in shape\nbut with some specialization  functions  as they develop.  They\ncommunicate  through a central connection  called the corpus collosum. In\nolder treatments  of epilepsy,  this connection  was severed and\nastoundingly,  the person functioned  very well even without this\nconnection.  Technically  speaking,  there are two people in one head if the\nconnection  is severed. It is a primitive  redundant  failover system in some\nrespects. One can extrapolate  from these results. Therefore  if you could\nshare brain signals from another hemisphere  even one from outside the\nskull the brains would grow together and learn to interpret  each other’s\nsignals. The real trick is to align the same stimuli to every hemisphere\nfrom the senses. The self organizing  nature of neural networks  with\nfeedback  takes care of the rest over time.\nThe military’s  interest in “psychic”  warfare” as it was called\nduring the cold war increased  dramatically  in the early 1960’s because it\nwas shown to be very feasible to accomplish  this same mind melding  feat\nat great distances.  The Russian’s  demonstrated  their technology  on the\n_\n2 The word “psychic”  was used as a discrediting  word. The modern day language is\nneuro-communication,  psychophony,  perception,  cognitive,  information,  and\npsychological  warfare technologies.Hacking Computer  and Biological  Systems Page |3\nU.S. embassy  in Moscow  in the late 1960’s but the U.S. didn’t want to\nshow their hand and acknowledge  it publicly.’  Additionally,  microwave\nwarfare occurred  in 1976 according  to a couple Army Intelligence\nofficers.  “The Russians  were beaming  complex  microwave  and ELF\nsignals to the United States, so we did the same back. The signals\napparently  were to calm the people of the US, as if we were the\naggressors.”\nOther scientists  both military  and private sector have successfully\nused magnetic  fields and coils near the head to influence  brain function.\nAnd the patent office is filled with brain modulation  technology  using a\nwhole range of radio frequencies  and microwave  frequencies  to affect\nand induce brain signal entrainments.  The technology  has come a long\nway since those days with refinements  to signal processing,  drugs, and\ngenetic  engineering.\nAnd of course the very gruesome,  invasive  brain chip implants\nhave proven extremely  effective  in both monkeys  and humans.  Both can\ncontrol robot arms or mouse cursors with just thoughts and conversely\ntheir brain signals can be controlled  by a computer.  But the most\nimportant  and lesser known  are the wireless  aspects of\nmind/machine/mind  interfacing  technologies.\nMind Hacking - The Enemy  Within\nThe exact number  of active U.S. DoD/NSA/CIA  mind hacking\nprojects  is difficult  to obtain. The number  of destructive  hacking  projects\nhas been reported  to be roughly 2,000* in the United States, 70 in the\nU.K., 30 in West Germany,  3 in Australia,  and several all over Europe,\nRussia, and Asia. Some researchers  total the people brought into this\nsecret army of remote control soldiers,  human experimentation,  and\nexperimental  interrogations  at 10,000 and others say it is much greater.\n* The truth behind the findings  are still classified.\n\n4|Page Project: Soul Catcher vol.2\nThere have been countless  books written by targets that describe\nthe experience  in detail. The interested  reader should review the\nrecommended  reading list at the end of this book for detailed descriptions\nof the subjective  experience  of being mind hacked by Radiofrequency\nHypnotic  Control.\nThere are some very prestigious  people who get abducted  into this\nprogram  who are currently  vocal activists  including  FBI agents, police\nofficers,  doctors, lawyers,  professors,  Pastors, Priests, and scientists.  You\ncan imagine  that with your new knowledge  of these technologies  that you\ntoo could control world leaders,  judges, and even members  of Congress\nwithout  them being too much the wiser. Complete  world domination  is\nnow within your reach. You just need a few billion dollars to build the\nglobal system. Knowledge  is truly power.\nAccording  to the Mind Hacking  Strategy  Group’, Ted Kaczynski\naka the Unabomber,  and the Oklahoma  bombers are obvious candidates\nto be checked  for a mind hack. Not even many years after the events\nwhich made them famous did anyone check them for bio-communication\ninfluence,  hypnosis,  splitting  of their personality,  nor to date has any\ncourt acknowledged  the ability of these weapons. Ignorance  is bliss and\njustice is blind. They make a lovely pair.\nHistorically,  mind hacking  tests have been written off by the\npurposefully  ignorant  news media catering  to the lowest common\ndenominator.  “Brain-nappings”,  as the cultish like human effects\nweapons  testing group of the Science  and Technology  Department  of the\nCIA enjoy calling it, have traditionally  been communicated  to the public\nas hauntings,  possessions,  evil alien abductions,  and in the recent\ndecades,  satanic ritual abuse cults.\nDiscussion  Questions:\n1.1 What ever happened  to paranormal  psychology  as a study in\nuniversities?  Research  what it was in the USSR and United States? What\n5 ‘They used to be called, “The Cult of the Mad Cow’ spoofing  the famous  computer\nhacking  group called, ‘The Cult of the Dead Cow’.Hacking Computer  and Biological  System Page  [5\nwas true and what was false? As you learn more in this book, recall how\ncover stories  work to confuse  the public.\nCognitive  and  Perception  Warfare\nDr. William  L. Baker  (Chief  Scientist)  and Dr. Eugene  J. Bednarz,  of\nthe Air Force Research  Laboratory's  Directed  Energy  Directorate,\nand Dr. Robert  L. Sierakowski  (Chief  Scientist),  of the Air Force\nResearch  Laboratory's  Munitions  Directorate,  wrote this article.\nat http://www.afrl.af.mil/techconn/index.htm,  Reference  document  DE-\n04-01.\nFor the Controlled  Personnel  Effects  capability,  the S&T (Science  and\nTechnology)  panel explored  the potential  for targeting  individuals  with\nnonlethal  force, from a militarily  useful  range, to make selected\nadversaries  think or act according  to our needs. Through  the application\nof nonlethal  force, it is possible  to physically  influence  or incapacitate\npersonnel.  Advanced  technologies  could enable  the war fighter  to\nremotely  create  physical  sensations  such as pressure  or temperature\nchanges.  A current  example  of this technology  is Active Denial,  a\nnonlethal  counter-personnel  millimeter  wave system  that creates  a skin\nheating  sensation  to repel an individual  or group  of people  without\n[physical]  harm.\nBy studying  and modeling  the human  brain and nervous  system,  the\nability  to mentally  influence  or confuse  personnel  is also possible.\nThrough  sensory  deception,  it may be possible  to create  synthetic\nimages,  or holograms,  to confuse  an individual’  s visual sense or, in a\nsimilar  manner,  confuse  his senses  of sound,  taste, touch,  or smell.\nThrough  cognitive  engineering,  scientists  can develop  a better\nunderstanding  of how an individual’  s cognitive  processes  (pattern\nTecognition,  visual  conditioning,  and difference  detection)  affect  his\n\n6|Page Project: Soul Catcher vol.2\ndecision  making  processes®,  Once understood,  scientists  could use these\ncognitive  models to predict a person' s behavior  under a variety of\nconditions  with the potential  to affect an adversary’  s mission\naccomplishment  via a wide range of personnel  effects.\nAs technology  has advanced  over recent years, most, if not all, systems\nare controlled  by, or include, some form of computer  or electronic\ncomponents.  Within the Dominant  Remote  Control capability,  the S&T\npanel investigated  the remote manipulation  of adversarial  electronic\nsystems to control vehicles,  sensors,  communications,  and information\nsystems. In one scenario,  the vision is to take control of enemy offensive\nand defensive  military systems (a spacecraft,  aircraft, or ground vehicle)\nand use them to our advantage.  It might be possible  to either confuse\nenemy systems  so they would be unable to successfully  perform  their\nmission  or to take control of enemy systems and remotely  manipulate\nthem. In another  application,  the control and manipulation  of an\nadversary! s communications  and information  streams  would cause\nconfusion  or provide false information.  The ability to disrupt or degrade\nan adversary’  s computers  and information  systems  could render them\ninoperable  or insert false information  which, in turn, would\nsignificantly  impair the enemy’ s ability to communicate.  If our military\ncommanders  could achieve this dominant  remote control capability,  all\naspects of the enemy’ s operations  in the battlefield  could be controlled  to\nour advantage.\nWithin the Controlled  Effects long term challenge,  the S&T’ panel\ninvestigated  the ability to tailor and deliver the most appropriate  type and\namount of energy onto targets of military significance  to create a desired\neffect. Scientists  are currently  developing  technologies  to enable a\nnumber  of first-generation  applications.  These include high-energy  lasers,\net\n. None of this can be done without  the ability to read a target’s  brainwaves  at a\ndistance and model it. It is an admission  to all the American  human experimentation  that\nthey have done.\n7 se stands for the Science and Technology  division of the U.S. government.  They\nwere formally  called TSS and focused on covert technologies  for the CIA such as drugs,\nweapons  development,  and interrogation  methods.Hacking  Computer  and Biological  Systems Page |7\nhigh power  microwaves,  micro air vehicles,  and some forms of\nantipersonnel  systems.\nThe article continues  with a cover story. What is important  to note\nabout this press release  is that by any scientist  who isn’t a chump,  the\nexplanation  of why it will take until the year 2025 to develop  is a\nridiculous  lie that involves  development  of anti-matter.  The only\nrelevance  to the development  of anti-matter  is that circularly  polarized\nbeams  used in neurological  warfare  create an effect called cyclotron\ngyromagnetic  resonance  which is also used in super colliders  which can\ncreate exotic particles  like anti-matter  through  acceleration  and collision.\n, The weaponry  is currently  being used and tested on thousands  of\nAmericans  and others around  the world. Our researchers  easily found 650\nnon-consensual  human  experimentation  victims. Many of course  have\ndied since the publishing  of this book and only have their testimony  and\nbee left behind  for us to study, uncover  the lies, and hopefully  set history\nright.\nLagnitive  Modeling  andReverse  Engineering  the Brain\nIn this thought  experiment,  we need to make a couple  of\nassumptions  again about sensitivity  of RADAR  imaging  techniques  to\nmake this approach  plausible.  Let us assume  that the sensitivity  of our\nmeasuring  technique  can measure  the creation  or disappearance  of\n300,000  ions per millisecond  with remote  sensing  techniques  which is\nfound in the depolarization  rate of one neuron.  Reading  the heat or\naverage  velocity  of an ion species  would  also reveal the brain signals\nthrough  frequency  spread  of Doppler  at many frequencies  that can\npenetrate  the human  skull. Also, one might  be able to measure  the\nconductivity  change  in the brain down to that of one neuron  through\nsmall resonance  changes*,  Using all four methods  would in\n\ncorrespondence  increase  the signal to noise ratio even further. In any ;\ncase, a precise  connectionist  model of the mind could be inferred  by this\ninformation.  Here’s how.\nA first or second order derivative  of the ionic concentrations  for\nexample  would show unique spikes every time an axon began its\ndepolarization  process and another  reverse spike when it hit the end to\nrelease  neurotransmitters.  It would be a rare occurrence  that two or more\nneurons  would precisely  coincide  at a starting  or stopping  cycle if they\nweren’t  related to the same thought  process  because  there is a small\nwindow  of opportunity  in time for two or more signals from different\nneurons  to arrive at the synapses  in order to correlate  negatively  or\npositively  to the next firing event. What one defines as the next causal\nfiring event has another  average  sized window  of time to be included  as a\nconnected  pathway.  These are possible  algorithm  for creating  MINDS,\ncybernetic  extensions  using frequency  and phase auto-correlates  of\nhuman  brain signals.\nThis algorithm  is included  on the CD which accompanied  this :\nbook (only available  on the teachers  addition).  There will be more detail\non this auto-correlate  matrix algorithm  later.\nLock and Key Mechanisms  for Brain Pathway  Bio-Amplification\nThe question  that most baffles  the common  citizen who has yet to\nexperience  the electromagnetic  virtual reality is, “Why don’t I feel\nanything  standing  next to a person who is being targeted?  Ifa brain cell\ncan be tampered  with by electromagnetic  energy, why don’t people go\ninto convulsion  due to all the cell phones and other noise?”\nIt is actually  quite a remarkable  feat that it can be done at all but it\nvery much requires  having  the exact right key and timing to hack a mind.\nLet us start out with some basic concepts.  If you put high voltage across\nanyone’s  head, they do go into convulsions  due to the electrical  current\ninfluencing  the neuron’s  ion flows and such. If you put relatively  strong\neffect” of ion density changes,  Doppler  spread, gyromagnetic  frequencies,  and cyclotron\nresonances,Hacking  Computer  and Biological  Systems Page |9\nmagnets  and pulse them next to a person’s  head it influences  neurons  and\nfiring patterns  and definite  changes  can be viewed  under  a functional\nMRI. Microwaves  at certain  frequencies  have been known  for half a\ncentury  to influence  neurons  both in a Petri dish and in the brain. So we\nhave several  mechanisms  that affect  everyone.  As a weapon  to be used\nover a broad area against  anyone,  microwave  weapons  are effective  and\ngo under  names like ADS and MEDUSA.\nSo one possibility  of how individuals  are targeted  with radio\nfrequency  synaptic  amplification  weapons  is the use of directed  energy.\nWe know that meteors  and missiles  can be tracked  all around  the world\nwith exact precision  at very high speeds,  it is quite feasible  to do it to all\nobjects  and reverse  the received  radar pulses  to send energy  to that very\nprecise  spot which  is called a “time reverse  echo”. However,  this is not\nenough  technology  due to the frequencies  that are needed.  Beam widths\nof large phased  arrays  still occupy  almost  a square  kilometer  once they\nbounce  the signal off the ionosphere  and back to Earth. This means\neveryone  in a square  city block is bathed  in the same signals.  Why can\none person  receive  the signal and others  standing  right next to them\ncannot?  Drum roll please.....\nPrecise  timing  of pulses is how the trick is done. Unique  human\nbrain signatures  are yet another  key to the locks that must be opened  to\ntarget a single  mind. The timing  of the pulses  must exactly  coincide  with\nthe end of a neuron’s  depolarization.  The Air Force accidentally\nmisclassified  and released  research  related  to finding  more UHF and\nmicrowave  frequencies  that release  neurotransmitters.  Neurotransmitter\nrelease  only occurs  at the end of the axon. See the diagram  below as a\nvery simplified  example  of why the precise  timing  of the pulse train,\nspecific  to each individual  and their microcircuits,  allows  the department\nof defense  to target  any specific  individual  for war purposes  or covert  use\nto instigate  war and violence.  This bit stream?  acts like an encrypted\nmessage  that only a single unique  human  brain with the exact physical\npatterns  can interpret  and whose  brain will amplify  the signal.  This is the\nbasic concept  behind the CIA’s synthetic  telepathy  capability  (bio-\ncommunication),  neural  reprogramming  (brain  washing),  and the cloning\n\nProject: Soul Catcher vol.2\n10|Page\nNetwork A Bit Sream\nNetwork. B\nNetwork  A is a simplified  example of what a neural network\nmight look like for a small feature. Each box represents  the basic unit ofa\nneuron which acts as an amplifier  and a threshold  comparator.  Ifan\nelectromagnetic  pulse of energy is exactly provided  during each Network\nA Bit Stream Key, only the brain which holds that unique key due to\nphysical  architecture  variances  can bio-amplify  each of the eed i.\nelectromagnetic  nudges to cascade it into an externally  stimulate iring\nof neural pathways  at the end. Note that the red lines do not align  at\nneural network  B’s moments  of “choice”,  i.e. their possibilities  of\namplification  of the brain signal. Similarly,  network  B s bit stream keys\nare unique and it would be extremely  improbable  that it would exactly\nmatch network  A’s. In the above example,  the probability  that another\nnetwork exactly matched another of the same size with that frequencyHacking  Computer  and Biological  Systems Pa\nresolution  is | out of 2°%, That’s extremely  improbable  even given current\nhuman  populations.  These unique  variances  of human  brains are the\nencryption  keys that allow one to “dial in” a specific  individual  and brain\nfunction.\nIn a couple  instances  you can see that the pulses  line up in\nnetwork  A and B. In order to create any significant  amplification,\nthousands  of neurons  if not more need to be exactly  pulsed  without  a\nsingle one off alignment  before  the electromagnetic  signal can gain\nenough  influence  in the brain for entrainment.  In other circuits  or brains it\nmerely  adds noise that is filtered  out. On top of the unique  fine structure\nof the neural networks,  the initial timing  of the beginning  of the sequence\nmust be precise.  So even if you had a perfect  brain clone, the brain’s  bit\nstream  patterns  need to be aligned  with the beginning  of some timing\nsignal to instigate  them.\nIn the government  test subjects  who have been interviewed  and\nexamined,  there are entrainment  patterns  to create the synchronization\nnecessary  to begin the correlated  bit stream  keys. Strobe  lights and\nbinaural  beating  effects  were used to create the brain entrainments  and\nhypnosis  in old CIA mind influencing  research  but the same effect can be\nachieved  through  other methods.  Many  targets  of this kind of\nexperimentation  say that they can hear a 3.3 hertz sweeping  sound,  a\nconstant  pulsing  tinnitus,  and see a very slight flickering  in their vision\nthat is synchronized  with the other two auditory  perceptions.  The reason\nfor this is that neurons  have an opportunity  window  to be effected  by the\nmagnetic/electric  field whether  ion cyclotron  resonance  catalytic  reaction\nor other methods.\nThe computer  neural  interface  can detect when the neural bit\nstream  key has been successfully  aligned  and amplified  by the feedback\nof neuron  depolarization  that comes  right after the pulse signal as an echo\nin the change  of ion speed concentration  and electrical  conductivity\nproperties,  i.e. an evoked  potential.  This is a type of brain echo effect.\nRadar  pulses  using the bit stream  key is sent to the target brain, and if it\nhits just right along with the others, a few microseconds  later an evoked\npotential  should  be detected.  This indicates  that the brain key is being\naccepted.  This is an important  feedback  mechanism  because  if another\nbrain begins to accept  the bit stream  keys meant for someone  else then it\n\n>\nis detected  and the power level can be turned down or other adjustments\nmade so that there is no cross talk between  neural links.\nThese bit stream keys are categorized  and sub-categorized.  Each\none represents  a “brain resonance”  or a state that was achieved. They are\ntemplates  that can be replayed  into the target mind. As the brain mapping\nprocesses  precedes  other bit streams fall into place into the whole\ncognitive  model faster and faster like when coming  closer to completing  a\njig saw puzzle.\nThe beginning  of cognitive  modeling  is the most difficult  part.\nOne aspect of this technology  first demonstrated  back in the 70°s by the\nStanford  Research  Institute  (SRI) was the ability to find the bit stream\nkeys associated  with phonetic  and word understanding.  It is far more\naccurate  than sound voice recognition  systems  and in the future will be a\nfar more efficient  way to communicate  to computers.  The bit stream for\nthe understanding  of the phonetic  sound can include  many sub context\nstreams  such as the physical  movements  of the tongue and mouth\ncorrelated  with the auditory  amplification  of those frequencies  when\ninitially  recorded  from the subject. This allows for the voice throwing\nventriloquism  tricks covered  in later chapters.  It is an essential  capability\nfor spy missions  and clandestine  operations.  And with even further\nrefinement  and processing,  just the bit streams  that convey  meaning  of\nwords can be played without  the other associated  sub-streams  and true\nsynthetic  telepathy  between  humans  and machines  and other humans is\nachieved.  Pretty cool, eh! We just have to plead with the agencies  and\nmilitary  to give up this secret weapon  and let the creators  show them\nwhat wonderful  and incredible  things we can do with it.\nThere are 6 billion brains on this planet each with nearly unique\nbit stream  keys for every major function  so in order to hack a human\nbrain you need to auto-correlate  all the bit streams  and map them into a\ncognitive  functional  model. It doesn’t  change all that much after the age\nof 23, so once mapped  the human  cognitive  model can be stored for\nfuture use, influence,  spying, etc. The interesting  calculation  to perform\nhere is that the average  human bit stream of consciousness  is somewhere\nbetween  2,000 and 2,000,000  hertz depending  on the number  of neural\ncommunication  channels  and neural firing resolution  desired  for the\nnetwork.  Most neuroscientists  look at EEG waveforms  which are all\nmost entirely  below 2,000 hertz however  when you include  the phaseHacking  Computer  and Biological  Systems Page |13\ninformation  (i.e. the slight  timing  offsets  of firings in related  groups  of\nneurons)  the bit stream frequency  would need to be increased\nsignificantly  to resolve  the differences.  So one can say that the entire\nhuman  race’s collective  consciousness  operates  somewhere  between  1.32\nTerabits  to 1.32 Pentabits  per second  (brain bandwidth  times population).\nThe entire entity, often called the geopsyche,  can be put into\nsupercomputers  and stored for eternity.  The computing  power  is here for\nsure.\nNow interesting  to note, most of the government  facilities  that\nhave the resolution  and sensitivity  to collect  this data from brains, such as\nthe Brazilian  and Puerto Rico lonospheric  Heaters  and Ionosondes  aka\nover-the-horizon-radar  aka mind hacking  radar, usually  operate  at 450\nmegahertz  and below.  These RADAR  systems  use an incredible  number\nof RADAR  imaging  techniques  simultaneously  including  a one second\nfrequency  sweep RADAR,  a fixed frequency,  pulsed  modes  operating\nacross  the full spectrum  and many more. They are capable  of tracking\nchanges  in ion density  created  from particles  of less than 5 hundredths  of\na microgram  traveling  at 60 kilometers  per second.  Think  about how\nsmall and difficult  that is. The facilities  have had this capability  since\n1960 with the first smaller  version  available  in 1948 a year after the\nformation  of the CIA. The cover story used for having  so many of these\n“meteor  observatories”  has two layers. This first cover story mentioned  is\nthat they are used to study the ionosphere  and if you penetrate  that story,\nitis said to be over the horizon  radar for the continental  ballistic  missile\nshields,  that that too is another  purpose,  but it is also capable  for the more\nominous  uses described  in this book.\nDiscussion  Questions:\n1.2 Academic  researchers  are generally  not allowed  to look at\nsignals  more than 20 degrees  from zenith when using these\nobservatories.  Why might that be? What happens  when one is\nunderwater  in a swimming  pool and looks up? Think about total\ninternal  reflection  off of atmospheric  layers.\n\n14|Page Project: Soul Catcher\noe sosean mae 2\n1.3 Imagine  if the swimming  pool somehow  was spherical.  How\nwould the curvature  alter the reflections?\n1.4 What are the main lock-and-key  mechanisms  which are necessary\nto target specific  minds like a mobile  phone call?\n1.5 Why are targets generally  driven away from each other in\npopulation  densities?  What would happen if two or more people\nhad very similar  minds and were proximally  near each other with\none on the bio-communication  spy network  and the other one\nwasn’t?  Would  secrets slip into the other mind?\n1.6 Can you think of a way to develop  human  minds over a lifetime\nto a standard  model so that a transform  into their mind could be\nachieved  more quickly  if their minds and bodies needed  to be\nused by psychic  intelligence  operatives?  Jumping  from one mind\nto another  sounds  science  fiction like, doesn’t  it?\n1.7 Discuss  metrics  that could be used to determine  the “closeness”\nof neural networks  and brains?  This is an advanced  question  for\nneuroscientists.\nGaining Access\nIn mind warfare  gaining  access to a mind just requires  time and\ncoordinates.  The mind has no firewall.  But in computer  hacking  it\nrequires  more subversive  tactics.\nMind VirusesHacking  Computer  and Biological  Systems Page [15\ncomputers,  a virus scanner  can't  just look for specific  byte strings  to\nrecognize  it. There is raw virus code included  in the CD for those\ninterested  in studying  them to possibly  find a better  way to stop these\nkinds of viruses  (Teachers’  edition).  In the mind virus space, the DoD is\nworking  to create polymorphic  autonomous  modification  viruses  for\nattacking  individual  and populations’  minds  based on biological,  nano\ntechnologies,  and computer  viruses.\nOne of the most malicious  viruses  would  be one that combined  all\nthe malicious  payloads  into one delivery  mechanism.  This is what the\nCIA research  into studying  mentally  ill people  has led to. Combining  all\nthe known  naturally  occurring  mentally  ill brain signals  has allowed  them\nto help the Department  of Defense  create very debilitating  and often\ndeadly  strains of mind viruses  using bio-communication  technologies.  In\naddition,  the strains  of mind viruses  appear  to mutate  a little during  each\nround  of testing  on the public  throughout  the decades  as the scripts  or\nprograms  evolve  and improve  their effectiveness.\nImagine  loading  up a portable  drive with hundreds  of computer\nviruses,  Trojan  horses,  and worms  and then giving  it to someone  that\ntrusts you. Even worse,  only the viruses  that are popular  ever reach the\norganizations  that add the strain to the virus checking  database.  Specialty\nviruses  and newly  written  ones will not be scanned  for by the popular\nanti-virus  tools. This insight  makes  this an easy way to hack into\ncomputers.\nThe mind has no firewall  and no anti-virus  software  so the public\nhas been left very vulnerable  to these kinds of psychotronic  attacks.  Only\noffensive  work has leaked  extensively  out of Russia  and the U.S. military\nlabs. There is little evidence  that any defensive  research  to protect  the\npublic  other  than in the private ", "metadata": {"category": "mkultra_benchmark", "topic": "mind_control_research"}}
{"id": "doc_82233726", "source": "psyco/Shapeshifting and Psychic Possession - Gangstalking Secrets of the Master Builders of Illusion (Eliza M. Parr) (Z-Library).pdf", "type": "pdf", "title": "Shapeshifting and Psychic Possession Gangstalking Secrets of the Master Builders of Illusion (Eliza M. Parr)", "text": " \nShapeshifting\nand\nPsychic\nPossession\n \nGangstalking\nSecrets of the Master Builders of Illusion\n \nEliza M. Parr\n \nCopyright © 2021 By Eliza M. Parr . All Rights Reserved.\nNo part of this publication may be reproduced, distributed, or transmitted in\nany form or by any means, including satires; photocopying, recording or\nelectronic or mechanical methods, or by any information storage and\nretrieval system without the prior written permission of the publisher ,\nexcept in the case of brief quotations embodied in critical reviews and\ncertain other noncommercial uses permitted by U.K copyright law .\n \nEPUB ISBN: 978-1-8381817-6-5\n \nFront cover: gang stalking woman shapeshifter and portal and all\nphotographs in this book were taken by the author while in the boroughs of\nGreater Manchester and Cheadle. The photo on the front cover has had\nelements sharpened, enlar ged, and realigned. This was for the purpose of\ndesigning a more streamlined thumbnail and not to mislead. The original\nuntouched photographs can be seen in their entirety in Chapter 12\nShapeshifting in Action-a full witness account with photographs.\nEliza M. Parr ©2018\n \n \n \nContents\n \nPreface\nIntroduction How The W orld Really W orks\nIntroduction (2) An Inter -Dimensional Symbiosis\nChapter 1  An Introduction T o Gang Stalking & St Theater\nChapter 2  Where Do They Come From?\nChapter 3  Portals And T ime Frames\nChapter 4  How Does The Shapeshifting W ork? 3d Printing W ith The Mind\nChapter 5  Imbibing Blood And Glowering Red Eyes\nChapter 6  Any T akers For Some Negative Ener gy?\nChapter 7  The Shapeshifted Forms Are T emporary\nChapter 8  Ufo’ s\nChapter 9  St Theater: Rituals In Disguise\nChapter 10 Through The Keyhole: A Shapeshifting Neighbor\nChapter 1 1 Things Are Not What They Seem\nChapter 12 Shapeshifting In Action\nChapter 13 Disguises And Deceptions\nChapter 14 Illuminati St Theater\nChapter 15 Their Concept Of T ime Is Dif ferent Than Ours\nChapter 16 Chi Is Everything\nChapter 17 The Currency The Gang-Stalkers Get Paid In Is Chi\nChapter 18 Possible Reasons Of Why W e Can’ t See The Shapeshifting\nChapter 19 What Do They W ant?\nChapter 20 Psychic Possession\nChapter 21 Is There A Spiritual Purpose T o The Gangstalking For\nEmpaths?\nAbout The Author\nOther Books By Eliza M. Parr\nI Won’t Cry For Y ou\nBibliography\nOne Last Thing...\n \nPreface\n \nAre they aliens?\nThey are inter -dimensional and dif ferent. They do not have the Chakras\nenabling connection to the universal oneness, God or soul. And as anyone\nwho has had the misfortune to come into contact with these beings will tell\nyou, they are incapable of love or empathy .\n \nThey come into being in a dif ferent way than authentic humans do and they\nare running a hive mind program that is all about hierarchy , power and\ncontrol of us, by their species. They are subservient to the mental ener gy\nthat controls their form and they can not think as individuals can. In that\nway they are certainly aliens to us, authentic humans, in the truest sense.\n \nBut their unfamiliarity to earth and us, is only seen that way because their\nexistence has been covered up by a (programmed) belief that tells us human\nbeings, the same as us, are running this world¹ and always have. But\nshapeshifters have been among us since the beginning of civilization and so\nin that sense, they are not Aliens.\n \nSeen from a wider perspective, many other unquestioned but accepted\nbelief programs about reality , can be seen too, to just be the creation of a\nmass acceptance put in place by an ongoing hypnosis through centuries of\npropaganda-by those in control.\n \nPropaganda, in